    <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Bent-Over Reverse Fly (Rear Delt Fly)</h1>
    <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>

This is an isolation exercise designed to target the back part of the shoulders, which is frequently neglected in standard chest and shoulder workouts.

 Primary Target Muscle: Rear Deltoids (Posterior Delts)—highlighted in yellow/orange in the animation.
 Secondary Muscles: Rhomboids, Middle and Lower Trapezius, and the Rotator Cuff muscles.
</div></div>

<pre>
<h1>

How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1> 

<u><b><h4>1. Starting Position</h4></b></u>:
 Sit on the edge of a flat bench with your feet flat on the floor, close together.
 Hold a light dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip (palms facing each other).
 Bend forward at the hips so your torso is resting on or close to your thighs, letting your arms hang down beside your calves.


<u><b><h4>2. The Execution (Fly)</h4></b></u>:
 Exhale and raise both arms out to the sides in a wide arc until your upper arms are parallel to the floor.
 Keep a slight bend in your elbows throughout the movement.
 Squeeze your rear delts and upper back muscles briefly at the top position.


<u><b><h4>3. The Lowering Phase</h4></b></u>:
 Inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells back down under control to the starting position.




<h1> Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Complete Shoulder Development:</b> Builds rounded, 3D shoulders by balancing out heavy pressing exercises (like bench presses and overhead presses).
 <b>◉Improved Posture:</b> Strengthens the posterior chain muscles that pull your shoulders back, helping fix rounded shoulders and computer posture.
 <b>◉Shoulder Joint Health:</b> Strengthens the small stabilizing muscles around the shoulder joint, reducing the risk of rotacuff injuries.



<h1> Recommended Sets & Repetitions</h1>

Rear deltoids are smaller muscles that respond best to controlled movement with lighter weights and higher reps:

| Fitness Level | Sets | Repetitions | Rest Period |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Beginner | 3 Sets | 12 – 15 Reps | 45–60 sec |
| Intermediate / Advanced | 3 – 4 Sets | 15 – 20 Reps | 45–60 sec |

> Pro Tip: Avoid swinging your torso or momentum to lift the weights. Focus on squeezing with the back of your shoulders rather than throwing the weights upward
